/**
 * @mainpage HelmBoy Documentation
 *
 * @section intro_sec Introduction
 * HelmBoy is a polyphonic software synthesizer built around the mopo processor
 * graph and JUCE application/plugin APIs. This reference combines the API
 * extracted from the source with the developer guides below.
 *
 * @section guides_sec Developer guides
 * - @ref architecture describes the repository layers, host lifecycles and
 *   global audio signal path.
 * - @ref state_and_parameters documents controls, host automation and patch
 *   persistence.
 * - @ref midi_input documents the active MIDI 1.0 path and the explicit,
 *   limited UMP decoder.
 * - @ref gui_and_threads describes GUI updates, visual snapshots and CPU-rendered components.
 * - @ref development_and_tests lists build targets and focused test options.
 *
 * @section source_layout_sec Source layout
 * - `src/common`: shared synth façade, controls, persistence and MIDI.
 * - `src/synthesis`: HelmBoy engine, voice graph and synthesis modules.
 * - `src/editor_sections` and `src/editor_components`: JUCE interface.
 * - `mopo/src`: processor graph, parameters and DSP building blocks.
 * - `src/plugin` and `src/standalone`: host-specific lifecycle adapters.
 *
 * The guides describe current source behavior; generated API pages provide
 * declarations and symbol-level details. Neither is a claim of runtime or
 * host certification.
 */
